<Base lang="en-US" pageType="CollectionPage" title="Martín Fierro Historical Archive — Manuscripts and First Editions" description="Explore original manuscripts, José Hernández’s letters, historical editions of Martín Fierro (1872 and 1879), and carefully identified archival sources.">
<article class="archive-en">
<nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/en/">English edition</a><span>/</span><span>Historical archive</span></nav>
<header class="head"><p class="eyebrow">ARCHIVAL DOCUMENTS · JOSÉ HERNÁNDEZ</p><h1>Martín Fierro: <em>the historical archive</em></h1><p class="deck">The history of a literary masterpiece survives in paper, handwriting, and printed editions. Explore authentic sources with clear distinctions between an original document, its reproduction, and a later bibliographic record.</p></header>
<figure class="banner"><img src="/media/fotografias-v3/archivo-documental-recreacion.webp" width="1300" height="800" alt="Modern digital editorial reconstruction of a historical document archive"/><figcaption>Editorial reconstruction, not a photograph of an archival collection.</figcaption></figure>
<section class="intro"><h2>What can these documents tell us?</h2><p>José Hernández’s literary voice is well known. Manuscript pages, letters, and early editions offer different kinds of evidence: the material process of writing, the private life of the author, and the changing history of the published text. A photographic reproduction is not the physical original. Likewise, a library catalog entry is not necessarily a complete facsimile.</p></section>
<section aria-labelledby="documents-title"><p class="eyebrow">SELECTED DOCUMENTARY RECORDS</p><h2 id="documents-title">Letters, notebooks, and early editions</h2><div class="grid">{records.map((d,i)=><article class="record"><a class="visual" href={d.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{d.image?<img src={d.image} alt={d.alt} loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer"/>:<div class="no-image"><span aria-hidden="true">✉</span><strong>Handwritten letter · 1865</strong><small>View at the custodian’s repository</small></div>}</a><div class="copy"><p class="eyebrow">{d.date}</p><h3>{d.title}</h3><p>{d.description}</p><p class="source"><strong>Source:</strong> {d.source}</p><a href={d.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{d.action} ↗</a></div></article>)}</div></section>
<section class="editions" aria-labelledby="editions-title"><p class="eyebrow">FURTHER BIBLIOGRAPHIC TESTIMONIES</p><h2 id="editions-title">Other editions and related writings</h2><p>These resources are useful for understanding the publication history, but their formats differ. A text transcribed from an old volume should not be confused with photographic pages from that volume.</p><div class="edition-list">{editions.map(d=><article><h3>{d.title}</h3><p>{d.description}</p><a href={d.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open institutional record ↗</a></article>)}</div></section>
<section class="method"><h2>Provenance and editorial integrity</h2><p>MARTINFIERRO.ORG does not own the manuscripts shown or linked here. Each item belongs to a holding institution or collection, and its reproduction rights must be checked separately. We identify contemporary illustrations as reconstructions rather than historical photographs.</p><p>Our Spanish reader contains both parts of the poem, comprising 46 cantos and 7,210 verses. Technical counts do not amount to a certified critical edition. Textual discrepancies between historical witnesses remain subject to documented collation.</p><p>Continue with <a href="/en/jose-hernandez/">José Hernández’s biography</a>, <a href="/en/what-is-martin-fierro/">an English introduction to the poem</a>, or <a href="/en/characters/">the characters guide</a>.</p></section>
</article>
